{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqgt5xujio3","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"/workspaces switcher list is over-inclusive: graphStore.allStores() accumulates transient workspaces, no existence filter","summary":"Found while verifying the per-repo dashboard live (task #1, merged d1abaa9). GET /workspaces (routes/meta.js) builds the switcher list by unioning the workspaces.json registry + state.workspace + sessions + agents + graphStore.allStores() store dirs. graphStore.allStores() retains a store handle for EVERY workspace read via ?workspace= during a daemon lifetime, so a one-off /state?workspace=<path> read (or a feature/attempt worktree the daemon served) leaks into the switcher and persists until daemon restart — even after its directory is deleted (confirmed live: a removed temp workspace still listed until restart; a fresh daemon restart then showed the clean single entry). The union also dedupes by exact string, so separator/case variants on Windows do not collapse. Recommended hardening: filter entries to paths whose dir AND .graph still exist on disk; optionally exclude the orchestrator worktrees/ tree and dedupe case-insensitively on Windows. The core ?workspace= per-repo data scoping is correct and unaffected — this is switcher-list hygiene only.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-16T15:39:55.675Z","vec":[-0.15027359127998352,-0.026557093486189842,0.002071298426017165,0.07903639227151871,0.03117436356842518,-0.0035205406602472067,0.007243202067911625,0.012159913778305054,0.007238306570798159,0.056049760431051254,0.04727393016219139,0.022645199671387672,-0.04244261234998703,0.05009628087282181,0.036900654435157776,0.0344797782599926,0.003488331800326705,-0.0609784871339798,0.03330337628722191,-0.05014573037624359,0.06538615375757217,-0.01663018949329853,-0.05236830562353134,-0.034946002066135406,0.012376419268548489,0.031296052038669586,-0.13507191836833954,-0.02507823146879673,-0.04446901008486748,0.022017398849129677,0.007440183311700821,-0.01